Description:
Novanet offers unparalleled experience in the area of terrestrial wireless communications.  Our experience spans mobile Broadcast ENG links to fixed point to point links.  We cover all frequency bands and content requirements.

Novanet offers regulatory support, path profile and system design, installation of the radio terminals and antenna, commissioning and after service support for wireless networks.

Our products and services range cover Security, Secure VoIP and Data Applications, to Licensed and Unlicensed wireless applications for Utilities and Enterprise.

Our Clients include Governmental Agencies, Project Management / Service Companies, Security / Monitoring organizations and Regional Municipalities for Water, Power monitoring and Control.

Novanet provides professional solutions for your growing and unique technology problems. We have a full complement of RF, IP and data engineers and specialists who can help on any technology related consulting or implementation project.

Our technical staff is professional, qualified and certified to offer the services including:
•Design of unique and custom transmission systems;
•Engineering services;
•Installation & Planning;
•System Integration;
•Monitoring 7/24;
•On going support & maintenance.

Once we have designed, and engineered a system, we can take over the full installation, planning and implementation of the project from logistics to system acceptance and sign-off.

Centre collégial de transfert de technologie en télécommunications.

Dans une perspective de développement durable, contribuer à la progression technologique et à l’essor des entreprises, organismes et maisons d’enseignement collégial. Plus spécifiquement, cette mission se réalisera en :

•	Entreprenant des projets de R&D;
•	Assurant des services de liaison et de transfert de technologies;
•	Offrant des formations spécialisées;
•	Mettant en relation différents intervenants et facilitant le réseautage;
•	Réalisant des études de faisabilité techniques et d’évaluation de potentiel commercial avec nos partenaires;
•	Organisant l’accompagnement des entreprises dans leurs étapes de réalisation de leurs projets d’innovation.

Solutia Télécom simplifie la mobilité de ses clients corporatifs depuis plus de 18 ans. Avec les plus hauts standards de service à la clientèle, Solutia allie la fiabilité du grand réseau Bell à la convivialité d’un service personnalisé et attentionné d'une PME. Guichet unique pour des solutions d'affaires en télécommunication, Solutia Télécom vous offre :

- Un service à la clientèle dédié et un suivi personnalisé;
- Une analyse en profondeur et l’impartition de la gestion de votre compte cellulaire pour optimiser les coûts ;
- La meilleure sélection d’appareil cellulaire sur le marché ;
- Des consoles de gestion pour votre flotte de téléphones (MDM) et un service de consultation pour choisir la meilleure console selon vos besoins spécifiques ;
- Un service de réparation de vos appareils ;
- Des appareils reconditionnés, déverrouillés et sans contrat ;
- La meilleure tarification du marché pour nos services ;

Solutia Télécom est le partenaire privilégié pour les entreprises en matière de services de télécommunication.

TEP Canada is the Canadian division of Tower Engineering Professionals.  Headquartered in Waterloo, Ontario, Canada, TEP Canada's qualified professional team offers:

•Site Acquisition;
•Inspections (audits, mappings, maintenance, lighting and post-construction);
•Tower, Mount and Foundation Design;
•Tower and Mount Structural Analyses to CSA S37 and ANSI/TIA/EIA 222; 
•Reinforcement/Modification Design;
•Rigging Plan Reviews; 
•Construction Installation Drawings;
•Electrical Design Drawings;
•Fiber Design;
•Geotechnical Investigations;
•Surveying;
•Anchor Corrosion Assessment and Corrosion Protection Installation; 
•Construction/Project Management;
•Tower Maintenance; 
•Tower Modification; 
•Tower Erection; and
•Design Build.   

TEP Canada’s management each have over 20 years of industry experience in design, analysis, inspection and construction.  TEP Canada's management is actively engaged in the governing engineering tower standards in Canada  (CSA Committee for S37) and the United States (TR14 Committee for ANSI/TIA/EIA 222).

TEP Canada places great emphasis on safety and training for staff including certifications for Tower Climbing Safety and Rescue training, RF Awareness, Wilderness Training, Defensive Driving and First Aid.  TEP Canada is actively engaged in both STAC and NATE.

TEP Canada has offices in Halifax, NS, Saint John, NB, Waterloo, ON, Calgary, AB, and Vancouver, BC.

Pelocom Inc. est une entreprise œuvrant dans le domaine des technologies de la communication. 

L’équipe expérimentée de Pelocom compte plus de 10 ans d’expertise dans ce domaine. 

Nous supportons nos clients à travers la province de Québec en leur garantissant une tranquillité d’esprit et une satisfaction totale.

Nous collaborons avec des partenaires reconnus et fiables apportant des expertises complémentaires et diversifiées à la fine pointe de la technologie. 

Pelocom assure une approche abordable et efficace visant la satisfaction de sa clientèle.

Nous offrons des solutions clé en main en prenant en charge l’installation, la configuration et le support de la technologie de communication désirée. L’équipe de Pelocom offre également du support et des services-conseils.

Pelocom propose des solutions, offre du support et des services-conseils dans les domaines suivants :

Téléphonie IP 4,0 Sur site ou hébergée;
Infrastructure réseau et sans-fil;
Vidéoconférence;
Communication unifiée et collaboration;
Support application mobile et web;
Hébergement;

Telecom Training Center offers the complete suite of technical services and well-established continuing professional development training courses for microwave radio PDH, SONET and Ethernet networks of any transmission requirements including mobile/cellular, Hydro, ISP etc.. Our goal is to contribute our expertise to the industry in the most economic and efficient way. Our training courses include:
  In-depth microwave transmission network design and Pathloss 5 training; 
  Microwave radio equipment theory, Practical application of design, implementation and troubleshooting training;
  UMTS/LTE cellular planning, design and optimization training;
  IP_MPLS network planning, security for telecom transmission.
  Practical in-field hands-on training in customer's network providing troubleshooting, maintenance and measurement
  Vendor specific equipment training: details upon request

We deliver the courses:
  in classroom in Montreal, Canada;
  On-Line via GoToMeeting;
  and at customer's preferred location.

The courses have been running successfully for 7 years, and are presented by leading experts in the field, drawn from academia, industry and service providers. We have served more than 70 companies across the world. Our mission is to provide world class telecom training, engineering design and consulting services, especially the course of the comprehensive microwave design program---PathLoss which has been recognized as the most popular microwave design tool in the world.

REMAC is a manufacturing company founded in 1986, specializing in the fabrication of aluminum and steel structures: viroles, marinas, docks, bridges, overpasses, custom structures, etc.
It recently launched a groundbreaking innovation for the telecommunications industry: self-supporting aluminum towers, ranging from 80 to 200 feet.
Aluminum allows these towers to: 
-resist corrosion; 
-be 50% lighter than traditional steel towers; 
-be prefabricated at the factory, which reduces the risk of errors and installation time; 
-easy to transport to remote locations; 
-drastically reduce TCO.
In addition, the towers are certified according to the Canadian standard (CSA-S37-18) and the American standard (TIA-222-H)
Contact us to learn more about our aluminum towers or any other products we manufacture!

